---
// site-pages 8.3. A draft that states only what the code does. Legal review is a launch step.
import ContentPage from '../layouts/ContentPage.astro';
import PrototypeNotice from '../components/ui/PrototypeNotice.astro';
import ExtLink from '../components/ui/ExtLink.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';

const toc = [
  { id: 'short', label: 'The short version' },
  { id: 'location', label: 'Your location' },
  { id: 'maps', label: 'Maps and links' },
  { id: 'ads', label: 'Ads and cookies' },
  { id: 'choices', label: 'Your privacy choices' },
  { id: 'logs', label: 'Server logs' },
  { id: 'analytics', label: 'Analytics' },
  { id: 'children', label: 'Children' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'Changes to this policy' },
  { id: 'contact', label: 'Contact' },
];
const H = Object.fromEntries(toc.map((t) => [t.id, t.label])); // headings and "On this page" share one list
---
<ContentPage
  title={`Privacy Policy | ${SITE.name}`}
  description={`What data ${SITE.name} uses, where it goes, and your choices. No accounts; your location stays on your device.`}
  path="/privacy/"
  h1="Privacy policy"
  lede={`${SITE.name} doesn’t ask who you are. This page explains what little data is involved and where it goes.`}
  updated="2026-10-12"
  toc={toc}
>
  <PrototypeNotice text="this policy is a draft, pending the owner’s legal review." />

  <section class="section prose" aria-labelledby="short">
    <h2 id="short">{H.short}</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No accounts. We don’t ask for your name or email to use the tools.</li>
      <li>Your location is used in your browser to sort places and is never sent to us.</li>
      <li>We don’t save anything on your device.</li>
      <li>Ads from Google, when we show them, may use cookies. You can choose how.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose" aria-labelledby="location">
    <h2 id="location">{H.location}</h2>
    <p>When you press Find places near me or Find free WiFi near me, your browser asks for permission. If you allow it, the page uses your position to sort places by distance. It isn’t sent to our servers or stored. You can turn location access off at any time in your browser settings.</p>
  </section>


  <section class="section prose" aria-labelledby="maps">
    <h2 id="maps">{H.maps}</h2>
    <p>The WiFi map loads map images from OpenStreetMap’s servers, which receive your IP address and the area you’re viewing, as described in the <ExtLink href="https://osmfoundation.org/wiki/Privacy_Policy">OpenStreetMap Foundation privacy policy</ExtLink>. Opening directions or a place’s OpenStreetMap record takes you to another site with its own privacy policy.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose" aria-labelledby="ads">
    <h2 id="ads">{H.ads}</h2>
    <p>To keep the tools free, we {SITE.ads ? 'show' : 'plan to show'} ads from Google AdSense. Google and its partners may use cookies to show ads based on your visits to this and other sites. You can turn off personalized ads in <ExtLink href="https://adssettings.google.com/">Google’s Ad Settings</ExtLink> and read <ExtLink href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</ExtLink>. When ads are live, we’ll show a consent message where the law requires one.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose" aria-labelledby="choices">
    <h2 id="choices">{H.choices}</h2>
    <p>When ads are live, you can review and change your ad and cookie choices here.</p>
    {!SITE.ads && <PrototypeNotice text="the privacy choices control from Google’s consent tool goes here when ads are switched on." />}
  </section>

  <section class="section prose" aria-labelledby="logs">
    <h2 id="logs">{H.logs}</h2>
    <p>{SITE.host ? `Our host, ${SITE.host}, keeps` : 'Our host keeps'} standard server logs, such as IP addresses, browser types and the pages requested, to keep the site secure and running.</p>
    {!SITE.host && <PrototypeNotice text="the hosting provider’s name goes here before launch." />}
  </section>

  <section class="section prose" aria-labelledby="analytics">
    <h2 id="analytics">{H.analytics}</h2>
    <p>We don’t use analytics on this site today. If we add them, this page will say so before they start.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose" aria-labelledby="children">
    <h2 id="children">{H.children}</h2>
    <p>{SITE.name} is for a general audience and isn’t directed at children under 13.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose" aria-labelledby="changes">
    <h2 id="changes">{H.changes}</h2>
    <p>When this page changes, we update the date at the top.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose" aria-labelledby="contact">
    <h2 id="contact">{H.contact}</h2>
    {SITE.contactEmail
      ? <p>Questions about privacy? Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.</p>
      : SITE.contactUrl
        ? <p>Questions about privacy? <a href={SITE.contactUrl}>Open an issue on GitHub</a>. Issues are public, so don’t include personal details.</p>
        : <PrototypeNotice text="the contact email goes here before launch." />}
  </section>
</ContentPage>
